From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:33:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cellPad tests: rumble follows the controllers that feed a
 port

Patch 4020 sends a port's rumble to the controllers that feed it, kept per
controller slot. test_pad_rumble checked that a request for a port with no
controller was kept; nothing is kept now (a controller plugged in later
starts with its motors off, as before). The test also checks the new case:
two local players with one pad, player 1's rumble (port 0, the keyboard)
leaves the pad alone and player 2's (port 1) reaches it.
---
 libs/input/tests/test_pad_rumble.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/input/tests/test_pad_rumble.c b/libs/input/tests/test_pad_rumble.c
index b5dec8a..af3abdd 100644
--- a/libs/input/tests/test_pad_rumble.c
+++ b/libs/input/tests/test_pad_rumble.c
@@ -65,9 +65,10 @@ static void test_set_act_direct(void)
     assert(vm_base != MAP_FAILED);
     s_pad_initialized = 1;
 
-    /* No controller on port 0: the state is kept, nothing is sent. */
+    /* No controller feeds port 0: nothing is kept, nothing is sent (a
+     * controller plugged in later starts with its motors off anyway). */
     set_act(0, 1, 200, CELL_OK);
-    assert(s_rumble[0].lo == 200 * 257 && s_rumble[0].hi == 65535);
+    assert(s_rumble[0].lo == 0 && s_rumble[0].hi == 0);
     assert(s_calls == 0 && s_rumble[0].sent_ms == 0);
 
     /* A controller: the request goes out at full small-motor strength and
@@ -93,6 +94,18 @@ static void test_set_act_direct(void)
     pad_poll_sdl2();
     assert(s_calls == 3);
 
+    /* Two local players with one pad: the pad is player 2's (port 1).
+     * Player 1 on the keyboard (port 0) does not shake it; player 2 does. */
+    pad_set_players(2);
+    set_act(0, 1, 255, CELL_OK);
+    assert(s_calls == 3 && s_rumble[0].lo == 0 && s_rumble[0].hi == 0);
+    set_act(1, 1, 255, CELL_OK);
+    assert(s_calls == 4 && s_lo == 65535 && s_hi == 65535);
+    set_act(1, 0, 0, CELL_OK);
+    assert(s_calls == 5 && s_lo == 0 && s_hi == 0);
+    pad_set_players(1);
+    s_calls = 3;
+
     /* A controller that goes away drops its port's rumble. */
     set_act(0, 0, 255, CELL_OK);
     assert(s_calls == 4 && s_lo == 65535 && s_hi == 0);
